r_own":2.9,"_gate_insider_buying":0.25,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":25.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"CME Group Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates contract markets for the trading of futures and options on futures contracts worldwide. It offers futures and options products based on interest rates, equity indexes, and foreign exchange; and agricultural, energy, and metals commodities, as well as fixed income and foreign currency trading services. The company provides clearing house services, including clearing, settling, and guaranteeing futures and options contracts, and cleared swaps products traded through its exchanges. In addition, the company offers a range of market data services, including real-time and historical data services. It serves professional traders, financial institutions, institutional and individual investors, corporations, manufacturers, producers, governments, and central banks. CME Group Inc. partners with FutureSports to futures on sports indexes. The company was formerly known as Chicago Mercantile Exchange Holdings Inc. and changed its name to CME Group Inc. in July 2007. The company was founded in 1898 and is headquartered in Chicago, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Terrence A. Duffy | Chairman & CEO | Age 67 | Compensation: $10.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $1.7M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $1.1M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $24K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["CME Group Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $113.8B market cap on $6.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 7% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $4.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 64 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.05\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 24\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Carries a 119% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.187647558787421},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (75% sell ratio, net $11.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 93% leaves thin coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"amber","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 11% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 36% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","22 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Learn Why The Bull Case For CME Group Stock Could Change Following Record October Volumes","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nasdaq-cme/cme-group/news/learn-why-the-bull-case-for-cme-group-stock-could-change-fol","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794590027.367,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why Wall Street wants to trade AI compute like oil","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/why-wall-street-wants-trade-233825990.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794613105.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Wall Street Slides As Chip Stocks Extend Selloff. Nasdaq Takes Biggest Hit Despite Cooler Inflation.","source":"ibtimes.com","link":"https://www.ibtimes.com/wall-street-nvidia-selloff-weekly-rebound-3809754","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794604715.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.013,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Wall Street Slides As Chip Stocks Extend Selloff. Nasdaq Takes Biggest Hit Despite Cooler Inflation","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/wall-street-slides-chip-